# mutgap3_sys_tracker_compact_keeps_runs: Compaction moves the runs a block keeps after the previous block takes its first ones. The fill of mutgap_mem_tracker_compact_stale_span: 128 blocks of 240 one-page runs at every other page of a 16 x 4096-page task, 200 runs unmapped in each of blocks 10 and 11, and a map near the end of block 127 that compacts: block 10 takes block 11's 40 runs, then 160 of block 12's, which keeps its runs 160-239. A lazy probe of old block 12's run 200 then finds it mapped (no map_memory call), as does one of old block 60's run 10; a probe of an unmapped page of old block 12 (run 20's neighbour) maps just it. Blocks only: the tracker exists only there (mutgap_memory.py's docstring); block calls as counts and a digest.
